
## Bandit Level 9 → Level 10


**Challenge:** 

The password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt in one of the few human-readable strings, preceded by several ‘=’ characters.

Commands you may need to solve this level
grep, sort, uniq, strings, base64, tr, tar, gzip, bzip2, xxd


**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: ls
# list files in the current directory
# data.txt should be present

STEP 2: file data.txt
# checks what kind of file it is
# this file is mostly "data" (not plain text), so we need to extract readable strings

STEP 3: strings data.txt
# pulls out human-readable text from inside a binary/data file
# output will contain many readable lines

STEP 4: strings data.txt | grep "==="
# grep filters only lines that contain several '=' characters
# one of these lines will show the password after the ====


```
**Password:** [FGUW5ilLVJrxX9kMYMmlN4MgbpfMiqey]


**USEFUL SINGLE COMMAND LINE**

strings data.txt | grep "==="

**What I learned:** 

strings command → “Extract readable text from a file that isn’t normal plain text.”

strings data.txt → prints only the human-readable parts

grep "===" → narrows results to lines that match the clue (several =)

